<!doctype html>
<!--
  The front.

  This path answered 403 until 16 September 2026 — the host's default for a
  directory with nothing in it. It was a deliberate open question rather than an
  oversight (docs/WEBSITE.md), and the answer turned out to be forced from two
  directions at once: an App Store listing needs a support URL a reviewer can
  open, and a domain whose whole purpose is carrying links looks broken when the
  domain itself refuses to load.

  **It shows the garden rather than describing it.** Until 24 September this was
  four paragraphs and four links, built from words the seedless `/s` already
  had. Marcus chose this in its place, design B of two prototypes (the other, a
  night, is `tools/wasm/web/front-a.html`):

  - one plant on a stage, turning under a finger — the child of a meeting,
    grown here by the app's own arithmetic;
  - how a plant comes to be, in three steps with a glyph each;
  - the ten areas as cards, each in its own ground colour with its glyph, what
    its plants mean and its name. The open ones come first and are links.

  It follows the reader's light or dark setting, as the pages of words do.

  **The plant is a demonstration, and nobody's.** Its two parents are minted
  from fixed words by `pg_front_meeting` (`tools/wasm/Sources/PlantWasm/
  Front.swift`), so the page shows what a meeting makes without showing a plant
  anybody grew.

  Static, like every other page here: no analytics, no font CDN, no third-party
  anything.
-->
<!-- `data-module` is stamped by index.php: the module's address with this
     build's mark on it, so a new one is a new address. -->
<html lang="en" data-module="PG_MODULE">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
    <title>Peace Garden</title>
    <meta name="description" content="A plant grown from a meeting." />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark light" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/assets/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/assets/icon-180.png" />
  </head>

  <body>
    <main class="page front" id="page">
      <!--
        The bar. On every page of the site, and the only way between any two of
        them that is not a link somebody happened to put in a paragraph.
        `site.css` §The bar says why it is the masthead with two things added
        rather than a header of its own. The mark is not a link here, because
        this is where it leads.
      -->
      <header class="masthead bar">
        <span class="bar__home">
          <img class="mark" src="/assets/icon.svg" alt="" width="44" height="44" />
          <span class="wordmark">Peace Garden</span>
        </span>
        <span class="bar__ways">
          <a class="quiet-button" href="/garden" data-s="gardenTitle"></a>
        </span>
      </header>

      <!-- The stage: the words on one side, the plant on the other. -->
      <section class="front-hero">
        <div class="front-hero__words">
          <h1 class="front-hero__title" data-s="tagline"></h1>
          <p class="front-hero__lead" data-s="frontLead"></p>
          <p class="front-ways">
            <a class="front-pill front-pill--solid" href="/download" data-s="downloadTitle"></a>
            <a class="front-pill" href="/garden" data-s="gardenTitle"></a>
          </p>
        </div>
        <!--
          Hidden until a plant is on it, so a browser with no WebGL2, or one
          that cannot fetch the module, is shown the words alone rather than an
          empty glow and a hint to drag nothing.
        -->
        <div class="front-plant" id="plant-stage" hidden>
          <canvas id="plant" role="img"></canvas>
          <span class="front-plant__hint" aria-hidden="true" data-s="frontTurn"></span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Three steps, as the app's first run has them. Monoline, even weight,
           round free ends, per BRAND.md §3.2. -->
      <section class="front-steps">
        <div class="front-step">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 56 56" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 14h14a3 3 0 0 1 3 3v24a3 3 0 0 1-3 3H9a3 3 0 0 1-3-3V17a3 3 0 0 1 3-3ZM33 12h14a3 3 0 0 1 3 3v24a3 3 0 0 1-3 3H33a3 3 0 0 1-3-3V15a3 3 0 0 1 3-3ZM26.5 24c1.2 1.4 1.2 3.6 0 5M29.5 22c2.2 2.6 2.2 6.4 0 9"/></svg>
          <h2 data-s="frontMeet"></h2>
          <p data-s="frontMeetBody"></p>
        </div>
        <div class="front-step">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 56 56" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8 18c3-5 10-5 12 0s-3 9-6 9-8-4-6-9ZM8 42c3-5 10-5 12 0s-3 9-6 9-8-4-6-9ZM22 22c8 2 12 4 14 6M22 46c8-2 12-6 14-12M40 30c4-6 12-5 12 2s-6 10-9 10-5-6-3-12Z"/></svg>
          <h2 data-s="frontCross"></h2>
          <p data-s="frontCrossBody"></p>
        </div>
        <div class="front-step">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 56 56" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8 48h40M28 48V22M28 34c-7 0-11-4-12-10 7 0 11 4 12 10ZM28 28c1-7 5-11 12-12 0 7-5 11-12 12ZM40 10a4 4 0 1 0 8 0M44 3v2"/></svg>
          <h2 data-s="frontGrow"></h2>
          <p data-s="frontGrowBody"></p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!--
        The garden: ten cards, each its ground, its glyph and what gathers
        there. Drawn by `frontpage.js` from `garden.js`, `gates.js` and
        `meanings.js`, so they are the map's areas in the map's colours, and
        each says what its area page and `/meanings` say.
      -->
      <section class="front-garden">
        <header class="front-garden__head">
          <h2 class="front-garden__title" id="cards-title" data-s="gardenTitle"></h2>
          <a class="quiet-button" href="/meanings" data-s="meaningsTitle"></a>
        </header>
        <nav class="front-cards" id="cards" aria-labelledby="cards-title"></nav>
      </section>

      <!--
        The foot mirrors the bar: one hairline, above it here where the
        bar's is below, and a row of two things at opposite ends — the
        privacy notice where the mark stands, the language where the way back
        to the garden does.
      -->
      <footer class="foot bar-foot">
        <a class="bar-foot__link" href="/privacy" data-s="privacyTitle"></a>
        <label class="chooser">
          <span class="label" id="language-label"></span>
          <span class="chooser__field">
            <select id="language" class="chooser__select"></select>
            <!-- Monoline, even weight, round free ends, per BRAND.md §3.2. -->
            <svg class="chooser__mark" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              <path
                d="M4 6.5 L8 10.5 L12 6.5"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.25"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
              />
            </svg>
          </span>
        </label>
      </footer>
    </main>

    <script type="module" src="/assets/js/plain.js"></script>
    <script type="module" src="/assets/js/frontpage.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
